---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import About from "../components/About.astro"
import AboutMe from "../components/AboutMe.astro"
import Cases from "../components/Cases.astro"
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro"
import Container from "../components/Container.astro"
import Cv from "../components/Cv.astro"
import Header from "../components/Header.astro"
import Main from "../components/Main.astro"

import CaseHogeschoolUtrecht from "../components/cases/HogeschoolUtrecht.astro"
import CaseQuaiDesNotaires from "../components/cases/QuaiDesNotaires.astro"
import CaseSamenOpStap from "../components/cases/SamenOpStap.astro"
import CaseSpeld from "../components/cases/Speld.astro"

import IconService from "../svgs/feature_service.svg"
---

<Base lang="en">
  <Header />
  <Main class="pitch">
    <About>
      <h1>Orchest &amp; Stef</h1>
      <p>
        I've spent most of my working life (15+) as a freelance full-stack
        developer. I've lead remote teams and I've worked on PHP/JS/React stacks
        for SaaS companies. As a freelancer I'm self-motivated and good at
        budgeting projects. I love your product and your vision and I think I'd
        be a great addition to your team.
      </p>
    </About>
    <Container>
      <section class="section">
        <p>
          I read about the job position on the Fronteers Slack, but the first
          time I read about Orchest it was on /r/selfhosted. I'm a huge
          selfhosted fan (I enjoy the podcast from Jupiter Broadcasting as well)
          and I'm just starting out with my own homelab at the moment.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's great that you are building an open source software with a 'open
          core' model. Although they have pro and cons, as a big open source
          user myself I like running these kinds of projects on my own homelab
          or on a VPS. I use Ubuntu as my main desktop distro and try to use
          open source as much as possible.
        </p>

        <p>
          I've downloaded Orchest and it's pulling the images as I type, but it
          looks like it might take a while and I want to share my CV with you to
          get the conversation going. By the time we speak, I'll have given it a
          spin.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'm specialized in front-end development, but I am pretty much
          T-shaped. I enjoy DevOps and back-end development as well, and like
          designing interfaces straight in the browser.
        </p>
      </section>
      <Cv />
      <Cases>
        <header>
          <IconService class="icon" />
          <h2>Relevant Projects</h2>
          <p>
            These are some of the projects I've done that are relevant to
            Orchest in some way. It could be because they showcase the tech
            stack you are looking for, it might be because they're bigger
            projects with a lot of customers or visitors, or they might be
            projects where I've taken on lead roles.
          </p>
        </header>
        <CaseQuaiDesNotaires />
        <CaseHogeschoolUtrecht />
        <CaseSamenOpStap />
        <CaseSpeld />
      </Cases>
      <AboutMe />
      <Contact />
    </Container>
  </Main>
</Base>
